  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\n1043 AM Update: Dense Fog Advisory has been cancelled. Previous\ndiscussion follows.\n\nDense fog has developed across western portions of the region where\ncloud cover has pushed east. Where cloud cover remains across the\neast, only expect patchy fog. In the middle, have patchy dense fog.\nCannot rule out that the dense fog advisory may need to be expanded\nagain. \n\nKey Message 2)\n\nMonday and Tuesday will generally be dry with precipitation holding\noff until late Tuesday into Wednesday. This will be the start of an\nactive weather pattern. Wednesday there are signals that there will\nbe the potential for a narrow corridor for severe weather Wednesday \nafternoon into the evening hours near the Ohio River. Wednesday night\ninto the early daytime hours the threat turns to more of a heavy \nrain threat. There will be another system on Friday where there will \nbe gusty winds and falling temperatures.",
